{"text": "injure", "etymologies": [{"etymologyHTML": "<p>A back-formation from <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"en\">injury</i>, from Anglo-Norman <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"fro\">injurie</i>, from Latin <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"la\">ini\u016bria</i> (\u201cinjustice; wrong; offense\u201d), from <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"la\">in-</i> (\u201cnot\u201d) + <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"la\">i\u016bs, i\u016bris</i> (\u201cright, law\u201d).\n</p>", "pos": [{"pos": "Verb", "definitions": [{"definition": "(transitive) To wound or cause physical harm to a living creature.\n", "quote": [], "relative": {}}, {"definition": "(transitive) To damage or impair.\n", "quote": [], "relative": {}}, {"definition": "(transitive) To do injustice to.\n", "quote": [], "relative": {"Antonyms": ["benefit", "help", "praise", "preserve"]}}]}]}], "pronunciation": [["Received Pronunciation", "/\u02c8\u026an.d\u0292\u0259/"], ["General American", "/\u02c8\u026an.d\u0361\u0292\u025a/"]]}